### --- phrazle ---
###
### { "data": {
###     "answer": "SNAKE EYES" },
###   "difficulty": 3,
###   "estimatedSeconds": 240,
###   "id": "2026-08-20:phrazle:abcd1234",
###   "type": "phrazle" }
###
### Wordle for phrases: guess the phrase, every guess a real word of the right length, four tile
### states instead of three. UNLIMITED ATTEMPTS -- see below.
###
### `answer` IS NOT A SECRET, and it is documented as one rather than obscured. The board paints its
### characters as tiles and marks them LOCALLY, so marking needs the letters. This API does not
### attempt anti-cheat and is not designed for it.
###
### It is the CANONICAL FORM -- uppercase A-Z words separated by single spaces -- and it is the only
### phrase-type answer that is not the corpus text verbatim, because the characters on the board
### must be the characters the marker marks. SPLIT IT TO GET THE GRID: the word lengths are
### `answer.split(' ').map((word) => word.length)`. There is no `wordLengths` field and there will
### not be -- two fields that can disagree is a board with the wrong number of tiles.
###
### THE BOARD YOU MAY BE HANDED, as of 2026-09-21: 2 to 6 words, each 2 to 9 letters, 9 to 30
### letters in total. The per-word cap came down from 11 and a 9-letter total floor was added, both
### narrowings, so a client laying out for the old bounds still renders every board correctly and
### NOTHING IS REQUIRED OF YOU. Two things in lull-ui are sized off the old numbers: the hint
### ladder's length cap in src/components/phrazle/rungs.ts, restated there as a literal 11, which
### is a ceiling on a rendered string and so cannot truncate anything; and any layout reserving
### space for an 11-tile row, now dead space rather than a bug. SEE RED and WING IT are no longer
### reachable answers -- an 11-letter row meant inventing an 11-letter word every day, and below 9
### tiles a guess buys too little feedback for the board to be solvable as an EASY puzzle.
###
### A renderer that assumes at most three rows, at most seven tiles, or a three-letter minimum per
### row is wrong on phrases this API already emits. TWO-LETTER WORDS ARE ORDINARY: OUT OF THE BLUE
### and PIECE OF THE ACTION are typical answers, not edge cases. Single-letter words are impossible.
###
### THERE IS NO GUESS LIMIT AND NO LOSS STATE. This type shipped a `maxGuesses` of six until
### 2026-08-24; THE FIELD IS GONE -- not zero, not null, not present-and-ignored. A player guesses
### until the phrase falls, and a board that runs out of rows grows another. Do not hard-code a
### limit, and do not reintroduce one client-side. Keeping a bounded window of guesses is STORAGE,
### NOT RULES: a client reading localStorage needs SOME ceiling on what it renders, but that
### ceiling bounds a corrupt write, not a game, and nothing on the wire declares it.
###
### `category` IS PRESENT ON THIS TYPE'S BAND 2 AND ABSENT ON ITS BANDS 3 AND 5. Read the key; do
### not assume either way.
###
### NO `hints` KEY, AND NO `phrazle-reveal` METADATA -- both removed 2026-08-31, both absent rather
### than empty, and the `kind` union no longer has a member for this type. The device now computes
### rungs about the LETTER ECONOMY of the phrase, against what the player's own guesses have ruled
### in and out: common letters the phrase does NOT contain, then uncommon letters it DOES, then one
### word's letters out of order. `answer` is all it needs and `answer` already ships.
###
### MARKING IS THE CLIENT'S, AND IT IS THE ONE RULE THIS API DOES NOT SHIP AS DATA. There is no
### per-guess endpoint and there will not be one: it would need a round trip per guess in an
### offline-first design, and nothing here authenticates a player. The rules are vendored as source
### (`src/rules/mark-guess.ts`, `src/rules/is-valid-guess.ts`) and hand-copied into the client. THE
### FOUR TILE STATES ARE ASSIGNMENT OUTCOMES, NOT MEMBERSHIP TESTS, and the difference is where
### every implementation of this goes wrong:
###
###   green   right letter, right position, right word
###   yellow  an UNSPENT copy of this letter remains in this word, at another position
###   purple  an UNSPENT copy remains elsewhere in the phrase, and none in this word
###   gray    no unspent copy remains anywhere in the phrase
###
### ONE PHRASE-WIDE LEDGER, debited by greens, then yellows, then purples. The passes run GLOBALLY
### BY COLOR -- every green, then every yellow, then every purple -- and strictly left to right
### within each pass. Running all three passes for word 1 before starting word 2 is WRONG: purple
### reads the phrase-wide sum, so it can spend a copy a later word's green is entitled to. For every
### letter, `green + yellow + purple <= occurrences in the answer`.
###
### A GUESS IS CORRECT IFF EVERY TILE IS GREEN. There is no separate comparison rule for this type,
### and adding one would create two definitions of "correct" that can disagree.
###
### A GUESS THAT FAILS VALIDATION DOES NOT COST AN ATTEMPT. Reject it at the keyboard: right number
### of words, right length per word, A-Z only, and every word in the guess dictionary from
### GET /dictionary/{version}, documented near the top of this file.
###
### PROGRESS: { "guesses": string[] } -- in order, in the same canonical form `answer` uses, and
### VALID GUESSES ONLY. MARKS ARE DERIVED ON EVERY RENDER AND NEVER STORED, so a corrected marking
### rule recolors old boards instead of contradicting them. `solved` is derivable: true iff some
### guess marks all green. THERE IS NO LOSS: the only two states are solved and still going. Prune
### progress WITH its pack, in the same pass -- a resumed board whose pack is gone has no `answer`
### to mark against, which is the one combination that cannot be rendered at all.
###
### --- end phrazle ---
