### 2026-09-07 -- THE SHAPE CHANGED AND THERE IS NO COMPATIBILITY PATH. `definitionSpan`,
### `fodderSpan` and `device` are GONE, with the two devices they described, "hidden" and "anagram".
### Every stored crypticclue puzzle was one of those two, so no stored cryptic is serviceable and
### the delete-and-rebuild runbook above is REQUIRED for that change.
###
### `clue`            the surface reading, rendered VERBATIM. Letters and single spaces only, at
###                   most 120 characters -- though the real ceiling is lower and varies:
###                   `explanation` quotes the definition and every cue out of this same string, so
###                   a charade clue tops out near 97 characters. It carries NO enumeration
###                   parenthetical -- the client renders `clue`, then ` (${enumeration.join(',')})`.
### `answer`          the solution, ONE uppercase word of 4-8 letters. Adjudicate through the shared
###                   normalizeAnswer rule, as on every other type.
### `enumeration`     word lengths, derived in code from `answer`, so it cannot disagree with it.
###                   Always length 1 today; the field is an array because the WIRE SHAPE is the
###                   expensive thing to change.
### `explanation`     THE POST-SOLVE REVEAL, rendered VERBATIM and never parsed. At most 100
###                   characters, and the only thing on the wire that says how the clue worked. IT
###                   NAMES THE DEFINITION: a charade and a deletion QUOTE IT FIRST, while a double
###                   definition takes no such prefix, because both halves ARE definitions and it
###                   already names them both. Three shapes:
###                     charade           "Floor covering" = CAR (vehicle) + PET (animal)
###                     deletion          "a mark" = BRANDY (spirit) minus its last letter
###                     doubledefinition  Two definitions: "Departed" and "still remaining"
###
###                   DO NOT STRING-SEARCH THE CLUE FOR THESE SUBSTRINGS in order to highlight them.
###                   No offsets are shipped, on purpose, and a cue is not always a literal slice of
###                   what it explains -- "vehicle" is in the clue, CAR is not.
### `hints`           ONE TO THREE RUNGS -- the only type whose ladder VARIES in length, and the
###                   reason the shared contract above says to read `hints.length`.
###
###                   THERE IS ONE POOL PER DEVICE and they do not share an order, because the same
###                   rung is worth different amounts on each. A charade always ships three. A
###                   deletion ships three unless its gloss dropped AND its definition is one word,
###                   which gives two. A double definition ships three with a gloss and two without.
###
###                   RENDER THE RUNGS IN ORDER AND DO NOT MATCH ON THEIR TEXT. A client keyed to
###                   "rung 1 is the device" reads the wrong sentence on most clues.
###
###                   THE GLOSS IS THE ONLY RUNG ABOUT THE ANSWER; every other one describes the
###                   clue. It is one sentence of at most 80 characters, model-written and gated
###                   here, and it may carry ordinary punctuation that `clue` may not. It is a RUNG
###                   and not a field: there is no `gloss` key on `data` and there will not be one.
###
###                   THE LADDER ESCALATES AND THE GIVEAWAY IS LAST. A rung that hands over the
###                   answer -- naming every charade part, or a deletion's source word -- sits at
###                   the bottom or is not emitted at all, so do not reorder the rungs and do not
###                   surface a later one first.
###
###                   NO RUNG STATES THE ANSWER LENGTH, because `enumeration` is already on the wire
###                   and the client already renders it beside the clue. If you stop rendering the
###                   enumeration, say so here rather than putting the length back in a rung.
###
### THE DEVICE IS NOT ON THE WIRE. Three exist -- charade, deletion, doubledefinition -- and the
### client is told which only in prose, inside `explanation` and sometimes a rung. Do not branch on
### the device; render the strings. There is likewise no indicatorSpan and no span of any kind.
###
### `category` is ABSENT BY DESIGN rather than hidden: the definition half IS the category, it is
### always on the wire because it is inside the clue, and hiding it is not available. Do not branch
### on its absence.
###
### `clue` IS STORED BYTE-IDENTICAL to the string the API verified. `explanation` and the quoting
### rungs are composed from slices of it taken at verification time, so a clue needing a trim is
### rejected rather than trimmed. Do not trim it, do not collapse its whitespace, do not re-encode.
###
### BEST EFFORT: this type is excluded from `complete`, so a missing crypticclue puzzle is never a
### reason to refetch. See the count table at the top of this file.
